<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end down, seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end down, seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed lower on Sunday and dealers predicted that prices would fall further amid lower domestic raw cotton prices.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Sunday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    500	    510</p>
<p>    Shafiq (Gold ky.)	  465	    475</p>
<p>    M.G.M.			 485	    500</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
